Package: h340-leds
Version: @VERSION@
Section: admin
Priority: optional
Architecture: all
Maintainer: Ehsan Enaloo <19691857+ehsanenaloo@users.noreply.github.com>
Depends: python3 (>= 3.11), smartmontools
Description: Acer H340 front panel indicators
 Drives the front drive, system and USB lamps of an Acer Aspire easyStore H340
 from disk activity, SMART health, system state, the fan tach signal and the
 front USB device. Only the measured H340 is accepted: the service checks the
 board and chip identity, writes only the documented lamp bits, verifies each
 write and restores the startup state on a normal stop.
 The bay of a disk comes from its SATA port. The service remembers which disks
 belong to the server: a disk joins when it is mounted. An unknown disk shows
 purple and a known disk that is gone shows a red fault.
 The service starts only when /etc/h340-leds.json exists. The openmediavault-h340
 plugin writes that file; it can also be written by hand.
